    "result_text": "There's exactly one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes. The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the welcome-notification side-effect on successful owner creation.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NotifyWelcome.java`: a single-method OfficeFloor step that reads the created `Owner` via `@Val` and emits an info line to the logger named `NOTIFY` containing both the owner id and the `memberId`:\n\n```java\nNOTIFY.info(\"Welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n```\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `notifyWelcome` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`, consistent with the rest of the pipeline) between `audit` and `respond`. It runs only after `save` (so the id is assigned) and `assignMemberId` (so the memberId is set), i.e. only on a successful create.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome`, which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and memberId, passes \u2014 as does the full suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Observed output confirms it: `INFO NOTIFY - Welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
